 \section{Related work}
 Test-time scaling studies compare prompt, sampling and search budgets \citep{wei2022chain,snell2024scaling,wu2024inference,alomrani2025budget}. Centralized allocation \citep{wan2026shadowprice} and confidence-based stopping \citep{jurayj2025finalanswer} ask different questions from service competition. Economic benchmarks study rational choice, auctions and interacting markets \citep{fish2025econevals,chen2024aucarena,zhu2024synthetic}; Bazaar studies repeated pricing with hidden preferences \citep{ahmed2026bazaar}. The contest in Appendix~\ref{app:servicecontest} draws on rent seeking \citep{tullock1980efficient} and compute-provider games \citep{artola2026games}.
 The main empirical addition is held-out economic scoring with a construction-calculator comparator, observable action-loss diagnostics and resource accounting. Appendix~\ref{app:servicecontest} uses that evidence in a conditional service-allocation sensitivity analysis; neither component evaluates an autonomous multi-agent market.
+Adaptive allocation is established prior work: FrugalGPT learns model cascades to trade inference cost against answer accuracy \citep{chen2023frugalgpt}, while Conformal Thinking calibrates reasoning stopping rules to specified error risks \citep{wang2026conformalthinking}. Decision-focused learning trains predictors for downstream optimization quality rather than prediction accuracy alone \citep{wilder2019melding}. Our prospective policy instead prioritizes extraction chunks using a bound on action-utility ambiguity and stops on conditional construction regret. It is neither a learned cascade nor a calibrated risk-control procedure; this operational distinction does not establish novelty priority or empirical superiority.
+Financial numerical-reasoning benchmarks include FinQA, which couples financial-report questions with reasoning programs \citep{chen2021finqa}, and TAT-QA, which combines financial tables and text with symbolic numerical reasoning \citep{zhu2021tatqa}. These motivate separating language interpretation from calculation. Our auction benchmark instead measures the consequences of selecting an action under supplied probabilities and a held-out price distribution; it does not test performance on either financial benchmark.
